                Short Help for the IBM-PC MBBS

List of commands:

BRIEF     BYE       CHAT      CLEAR     CLOCK     COUNT
DAYFILE   DEFINE    END       HELP      LIST      MAIL
QUIT      PAUSE     READ      SEND      SKIM      STATUS
TOPIC     UNJOIN    USERS     VOTE      WRITE


     Pressing the ESC key will erase the current line.  Pressing
the S-key will stop the display.  Pressing the I-key will inter-
rupt the display.


                  Long Help for the IBM-PC MBBS

        The following is a full list of commands:

        BRIEF - Toggles brief mode.

        BYE - Leave the system.

        CHAT - Talk with the system operator.

        CLEAR - Erase old mailbox messages.

        CLOCK - Get the current time and date.

        COUNT - Count the votes of users for/against the
                current proposal.

        DAYFILE - See who has been logging in lately.

        DEFINE - Define new login parameters.

        END - Leave the system.

        HELP - Obtain this display.

        LIST - List all available topics.

        MAIL - Toggle mail mode.  In this mode the
               READ and WRITE commands send to specific
               individuals rather than to public topic
               files.

        QUIT - Leave the system.

        PAUSE - Toggles pause mode.

        READ <number> - Initiate reading of
             a topic file starting at given message
             number.  If you have no current topic, then
             you will be prompted for it.  If you omit
             the message number, then you will start reading
             where you last left off.  This command also
             reads your private messages if you are in
             mail mode.

        SEND <topic> - Write a message and send it to
             the given topic.  If you omit the topic name,
             then the current topic is selected.  This
             command is used to send private messages
             if you are in mail mode.

        SKIM - Toggles skim mode.  Only the first two lines
               of each message are displayed.

        STATUS - Show your status bits for PAUSE, SKIM,.
                 and BRIEF; and give the current
                 selected topic name.

        TOPIC <name> - Select a topic for reading
              and writing.  If you dont specify
              the name then you will be prompted
              for it.

        UNJOIN - Remove your name from the users list.

        USERS - Display the names of all active users.

        VOTE  - Place a vote for/against the current
                proposal.

        WRITE <topic> - Same as the SEND command (see above).

        <number> - Entering just a number will cause the selected
                   message to be printed.


        While you are entering a message, you may edit it using
the following special edit commands:

        ^D       - Delete the previous line.
        ^O or ^A - Abort the message.
        ^P or ^L - Print the message for inspection.

        Each message may be up to 80 characters wide and 25 lines long.

        1200 baud users:  Please use 8 data bits, 1 stop bit, and
                          no parity for best results.

        If you have any questions, please direct them to AEK on
the MBBS mail service.  Thank you!
